# tests/base/cls_fold.rxt — [FORM-CHAR] STEP 1: the VM's ASCII-FOLD class
# test (docs/spec/tuning.md §2.22), as ANSWERS.
#
# Every pattern here is CAPTURE-BEARING on purpose: a capture routes the
# default compile to the VM, which is the one engine `vm_cls_shape`'s fold
# form reaches — a capture-free caseless literal is a DFA artifact and
# exercises nothing this file is about. The pairs of blocks are the two
# sides of the recognizer:
#
#   - a class that IS an ASCII fold pair ([Aa], [Zz], and what (?i) makes of
#     a letter) takes the fold compare `(byte | 0x20) == lower`;
#   - a two-member class that is NOT one ([ac] — same size, not a 0x20-pair)
#     keeps the bitmap, and its cells are the CONTROL population: sabotage
#     S228 (the recognizer widened to any two-member set) loses `ax`'s match
#     in the first block below while every fold-pair block stays green.
#
# The `` `x ``/`@x` cells pin the fold CONSTANT: 0x60/0x40 are the letters'
# 0x20-neighbours one bit off, so an off-by-one-bit compare admits them.
#
# All expectations python3-re verified (2026-09-05, this file's authoring
# sweep; re.search spans and group spans, transcribed unmodified).

# case: fold-control-nonpair
pattern ([ac])x
# {a,c}: two members, NOT a 0x20-pair — stays on the bitmap. S228's detector.
m "ax" 0 2
g 1 0 1
m "cx" 0 2
g 1 0 1
n "Cx"
n "bx"
m "xax" 1 3
g 1 1 2
m "acx" 1 3
g 1 1 2

# case: fold-pair-explicit
pattern ([Aa])x
# {A,a} spelled as a class, no caseless flag anywhere: the SET is what the
# recognizer reads, not where it came from.
m "Ax" 0 2
g 1 0 1
m "ax" 0 2
g 1 0 1
n "bx"
n "@x"
n "`x"
m "Zax" 1 3
g 1 1 2

# case: fold-pair-caseless-inline
pattern (?i)(q)r
# what D23's parse-time folding makes of a caseless letter — two fold-pair
# positions, one captured.
m "qr" 0 2
g 1 0 1
m "QR" 0 2
g 1 0 1
m "Qr" 0 2
g 1 0 1
m "qR" 0 2
g 1 0 1
n "xr"
m "aQRb" 1 3
g 1 1 2

# case: fold-pair-quantified
pattern ([Zz]){2,4}y
# the fold class under a counted repeat: the shape rides whichever rung the
# quantifier takes, and the LAST iteration's capture is what survives.
m "zZy" 0 3
g 1 1 2
m "ZzzZy" 0 5
g 1 3 4
n "Zy"
m "zzzzzy" 1 6
g 1 4 5
n "ay"

# case: fold-and-nonpair-mixed
pattern ([Aa])([ac])d
# one artifact holding BOTH shapes: a fold class and a bitmap class whose
# members overlap on 'a' — cross-class confusion is a wrong answer here.
m "Aad" 0 3
g 1 0 1
g 2 1 2
m "acd" 0 3
g 1 0 1
g 2 1 2
n "AAd"
n "aCd"
m "xacd" 1 4
g 1 1 2
g 2 2 3

# case: fold-chain-uncaptured
pattern ((?i:abc))
# the family-A witness shape itself, captured so the default engine is the
# VM: three fold-pair positions in a row — the literal chain the form
# exists to keep.
m "abc" 0 3
g 1 0 3
m "ABC" 0 3
g 1 0 3
m "aBc" 0 3
g 1 0 3
n "abd"
m "xAbCy" 1 4
g 1 1 4
